NNAAMMEE
       savelog - save a log file

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ssaavveelloogg  [-m  mode] [-u user] [-g group] [-t] [-p] [-c cycle] [-l] [-j]
       [-J] [-1 .. -9] [-C] [-d] [-l] [-r rolldir] [-n] [-q]  [-D  dateformat]
       file ...

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ssaavveelloogg  command  saves  and  optionally  compresses old copies of
       files.  Older versions of _f_i_l_e are named:

              _f_i_l_e._<_n_u_m_b_e_r_>_<_c_o_m_p_r_e_s_s___s_u_f_f_i_x_>

       where _<_n_u_m_b_e_r_> is the version number, 0 being the newest.  Version num‐
       bers > 0 are compressed unless --ll prevents it.  Version number 0 is not
       compressed because a process might still  have  _f_i_l_e  opened  for  I/O.
       Only _c_y_c_l_e versions of the file are kept.

       If the file does not exist and --tt was given, it will be created.

       For files that do exist and have lengths greater than zero, the follow‐
       ing actions are performed:


       1)     Version numbered files are cycled.  Version _f_i_l_e..22 is  moved  to
              version  _f_i_l_e..33,  version _f_i_l_e..11 is moved to version _f_i_l_e..22, and
              so on.  Finally version _f_i_l_e..00 is moved to version  _f_i_l_e..11,  and
              version _f_i_l_e is deleted.  Both compressed names and uncompressed
              names are cycled, regardless of --ll.  Missing version  files  are
              ignored.

       2)     The  new  _f_i_l_e..11 is compressed unless the --ll flag was given.  It
              is changed subject to the --mm, --uu, and --gg flags.

       3)     The main _f_i_l_e is moved to _f_i_l_e..00.

       4)     If the --mm, --uu, --gg,  --tt, or --pp flags are  given,  then  an  empty
              _f_i_l_e  is  created subject to the given flags.  With the --pp flag,
              the file is created with the same owner, group, and  permissions
              as before.

       5)     The new _f_i_l_e..00 is changed subject to the --mm, --uu, and --gg flags.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --mm mmooddee
              chmod the log files to mode, implies --tt

       --uu uusseerr
              chown log files to user, implies --tt

       --gg ggrroouupp
              chgrp log files to group, implies --tt

       --cc ccyyccllee
              Save  cycle  versions  of  the  logfile (default: 7).  The _c_y_c_l_e
              count must be at least 2.

       --tt     touch new logfile into existence

       --ll     don't compress any log files (default: do compress)

       --pp     preserve owner, group, and permissions of logfile

       --jj     compress with bzip2 instead of gzip

       --JJ     compress with xz instead of gzip

              For xz no strength option is set, and xz decides on the  default
              based on the total amount of physical RAM.  Note that xz can use
              a very large amount of memory for the higher compression levels.

       --11 .... --99
              compression strength or memory usage (default: 9, except for xz)

       --CC     force cleanup of cycled logfiles

       --dd     use standard date for rolling

       --DD ddaatteeffoorrmmaatt
              override date format, in the syntax understood  by  the  ddaattee(1)
              command

       --rr     use _r_o_l_l_d_i_r instead of . to roll files

       --nn     do not rotate empty files

       --qq     be quiet

BBUUGGSS
       If a process is still writing to _f_i_l_e..00, and savelog moves it to _f_i_l_e..11
       and compresses it, data could be lost.

